# qemu/tpm-board-aarch64.pins: the aarch64 TPM board's inputs (1.11.1).
#
# Debian trixie arm64 packages from snapshot.debian.org, all under one timestamp. A
# file under a snapshot timestamp never changes, so these cannot move the way Alpine's
# mirror does (standing rules 50, 52). Each line is `<sha256> <path under base>`, and a
# download that does not match its sum is a failure, never a retry.
#
# The kernel is Debian's cloud flavour, and only this pass boots it. Neither Alpine
# aarch64 kernel builds a TPM TIS driver (CONFIG_TCG_TIS is unset in lts and virt), so
# no QEMU TPM can appear on the board the other passes boot.
#
# The firmware is Debian's AAVMF, because PCR 7 is what firmware measures and a kernel
# QEMU starts directly has none: PCR 7 reads all-zero, which kybernet treats as an
# unread PCR, never a match. Only the secure-boot-capable AAVMF build has TPM2 support
# (edk2's debian/rules gives -DTPM2_ENABLE to that build and not to no-secboot). Its
# empty variable store leaves secure boot in setup mode, so nothing is enforced.
#
# The other 58 packages hold the shared-library closure of veritysetup, cryptsetup,
# tpm2-tools and systemd's LUKS2 TPM2 token plugin, plus the tpm2-tss libraries the
# plugin dlopen()s and glibc's libgcc_s: only packages that ship a file the board
# loads. The harness checks that closure again on every run. Moving the snapshot means
# changing every line.
base https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20261001T000000Z
